From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] quartz: filter graph IMediaSeeking rate/preroll/available, IMediaPosition, IGraphConfig, IVideoFrameStep, IMediaFilter::GetClassID

quartz's filter graph manager: the IMediaSeeking, IMediaPosition,
IGraphConfig, IVideoFrameStep and IMediaFilter members that were stubs.

- IMediaSeeking::SetRate sends the rate to every seekable filter (an error
  other than E_NOTIMPL from one is returned and keeps the old rate); with no
  filter able to change speed only 1.0 is accepted, anything else is
  E_NOTIMPL. GetRate returns the rate last set (1.0 at first).
  GetPreroll is the largest preroll of the filters (E_NOTIMPL when none
  has one), GetAvailable the range every filter can reach.
  QueryPreferredFormat is always media time and no longer logs a FIXME.
- IMediaPosition::get_PrerollTime converts GetPreroll to seconds,
  put_PrerollTime is E_NOTIMPL (IMediaSeeking has no way to set it),
  CanSeekForward/Backward report the graph's seeking capabilities as
  OATRUE/OAFALSE.
- IMediaFilter::GetClassID returns CLSID_FilterGraph, or
  CLSID_FilterGraphNoThread for the graph made without a thread.
- IGraphConfig: AddFilterToCache / EnumCacheFilter / RemoveFilterFromCache
  keep a reference-counted cache of filters, per-filter flags
  (SetFilterFlags / GetFilterFlags, AM_FILTER_FLAGS_REMOVABLE only),
  GetStartTime returns the time the graph last started streaming,
  Reconnect disconnects and reconnects a pair of pins (a missing pin is the
  peer of the other; DIRECTCONNECT, a filter to go through, cached filters,
  a type for the first connection, an abort event; the old connection is put
  back on failure), RemoveFilterEx with REMFILTERF_LEAVECONNECTED joins the
  neighbours of the removed filter, PushThroughData asks the sink to report
  the end of the stream on the event.
- IVideoFrameStep forwards Step / CanStep / CancelStep to the first filter
  (or the filter or pin given) that supports it: CanStep is S_FALSE and
  Step E_NOTIMPL when none does.
- IMediaControl::AddSourceFilter, FilterCollection and RegFilterCollection
  need the automation collection objects that do not exist here; they now
  return E_NOTIMPL with a NULL result instead of a fake success.
- The conformance tests' todo_wine for GetAvailable, SetRate, GetRate and
  GetPreroll are removed.

